## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design region-isolated pipelines, governance, and controlled rollouts with evidence of explainability, drift handling, and rollback—key for production ML in regulated environments.

## Key Concepts
- Data locality: regional storage and training
- Pipeline orchestration: Pub/Sub, Dataflow, Vertex AI
- Model governance: lineage in BigQuery, drift alerts
- Explainability: Vertex Explainable AI
- Rollback: blue/green deployment

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: Dataflow route and validate
if (record.region && isValid(record)) {
  writeToCloudStorage(record, `/region/${record.region}/data.json`);
} else {
  logError(record);
}
```
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the rollback path in a pre-prod environment?
- What would you monitor to distinguish drift from data quality issues?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect end-to-end edge ML workflows on GCP with enterprise-grade privacy, governance, and operational considerations beyond model accuracy.

## Key Concepts
- Edge model distillation and Vertex AI training pipelines
- Edge artifact distribution via Pub/Sub and Cloud CDN
- Regional canary deployments and per-tenant quotas
- Data residency, CMEK, and DLP for privacy compliance
- On-device telemetry, drift monitoring, and automated rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example config for edge rollout policy
const rollout = {
  region: 'us-east1',
  quota: 1000,
  canary: {
    percentage: 10,
    duration: '2h'
  },
  validation: {
    latencyTarget: '<100ms',
    driftThreshold: 0.05,
    minSampleSize: 1000
  },
  rollback: {
    auto: true,
    cooldown: '30min'
  }
};
```
